1. e4 c5 2. c3 Nf6 3. e5 Nd5 4. d4 cxd4 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. cxd4
6... Nb6? { The knight goes back without first playing ...d6, so nothing hits the pawn on e5 and nothing stops White's next move. }
7. d5! { Attacks the knight on c6. If it takes on e5, White's knight takes it back and Black has lost a knight for a pawn. }
7... Nb4
(7... Nxe5 8. Nxe5)
